######## code-health-rules
The default code health rules should be suitable for most codebases but
sometimes it can be helpful to tweak certain thresholds or weights.

The rules are customized by adding .codescene/code-health-rules.json file to
your git repository. That way, the code health rules are persisted and
version-controlled together with the application code they apply to.

You can get a template with all available rules to tweak by issuing:

    $ cs docs code-health-rules-template

Or, assuming you are in the root directory of your git repository, redirect it
to the right place immediately:

    $ cs docs code-health-rules-template > .codescene/code-health-rules.json

Then edit it to your liking.

You can also read more at: https://codescene.io/docs/guides/technical/code-health.html#adapt-code-health-to-your-coding-standards

